---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
const updated = '5 September 2026'
---

<Base
  title="Privacy — what this site collects"
  description="What ephesushq.com collects and what it does not: two cookieless analytics services, no consent banner because nothing is stored on your device, nothing sold.">

  <section class="pagehead">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <span class="eyebrow">Privacy</span>
      <h1>What this site collects</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Short version: <strong>no cookies are set</strong>, no account exists, nothing is sold, and
        two analytics services count visits without identifying you — Vercel Web Analytics, which is
        cookieless by design, and Google Analytics, configured to store nothing on your device.
      </p>
      <p class="updated">Last updated {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        Two services count visits here, and <strong>neither writes a cookie or builds a profile of
        you</strong>.
      </p>

      <h3>Vercel Web Analytics</h3>
      <p>
        Provided by the host that serves this site. It is <strong>cookieless by design rather than
        by configuration</strong>: it sets nothing on your device, assigns you no identifier, and
        cannot follow you between sites or between visits. It records that a page was requested,
        which page referred it, and a coarse country — and derives a per-day hash from request
        headers that is discarded daily and cannot be reversed to identify you.
      </p>
      <p>
        It is here because the Google tag below, configured as it is, reports almost nothing: with
        no identifier to work from, Google estimates visits through behavioural modelling, and that
        modelling needs roughly a thousand consented events a day before it activates. This site
        does not reach that, so a second, simpler counter does the job the first one cannot.
      </p>

      <h3>Google Analytics 4</h3>
      <p>
        Runs with <strong>Google Consent Mode v2, with every storage type denied by default</strong>:
      </p>
      <pre><code>ad_storage            denied
ad_user_data          denied
ad_personalization    denied
analytics_storage     denied</code></pre>
      <p>
        Because analytics storage is denied, <strong>no analytics cookies are written to your
        device and no persistent identifier is created for you</strong>. Google receives an
        anonymous, aggregated signal — that a page was viewed, roughly where from, and what referred
        it — with no way to link it to you across visits. IP addresses are anonymised before
        storage.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>That is why there is no consent banner.</strong> A banner exists to ask permission to
        store things on your device. Neither service stores anything on your device, so there is
        nothing to ask you for.
      </p>

      <h2>What is not collected</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No account, login, or profile — there is nothing to sign up for.</li>
        <li>No contact form, newsletter, or email capture.</li>
        <li>No advertising, remarketing, or cross-site tracking.</li>
        <li>No session recording, heatmaps, or scroll tracking.</li>
        <li>No data is ever sold, rented, or shared with anyone beyond the two analytics providers and the host named here.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Fonts and assets</h2>
      <p>
        All fonts are <strong>self-hosted on this domain</strong>. Loading a page here makes no
        request to Google Fonts, so no request from your browser reaches a font CDN and no IP
        address is disclosed to one. Every image, stylesheet and script is served from
        <code>ephesushq.com</code> apart from the two analytics tags named above: Google&rsquo;s, which
        loads from <code>googletagmanager.com</code>, and Vercel&rsquo;s, which loads from
        <code>/_vercel/insights/</code> on this same domain.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The site is static and hosted on Vercel, which processes standard server request data — IP
        address, user agent, requested URL — to deliver pages and defend against abuse. That is
        ordinary web-server operation and is not used to profile you.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under the GDPR and Turkey&rsquo;s KVKK you may ask what data relating to you is held, and ask
        for it to be corrected or erased. Given the above there is realistically nothing to retrieve
        — no identifier for you exists — but the request is welcome and will be answered honestly.
        Write to <a href="mailto:sensoymertefe@gmail.com">sensoymertefe@gmail.com</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can also block analytics entirely with any content blocker, or by enabling
        &ldquo;Do Not Track&rdquo;. Nothing on this site is withheld from you if you do.
      </p>

      <h2>The software</h2>
      <p>
        This page is about the website. <strong>The Ephesus application is different</strong>: it
        runs entirely on your own machine, has no telemetry, and sends nothing anywhere. It drives
        agent CLIs that are already installed on your computer; whatever those send to their vendors
        is governed by their own terms and is unchanged by Ephesus being in front of them.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this changes, the date at the top changes with it, and the change is in the
        <a href="https://github.com/Cassandra-Collective/Ephesus/commits/main/site/src/pages/privacy.astro">git history of this page</a>
        like everything else here.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .pagehead { padding: 62px 0 40px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--paper-3); }
    .updated { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; color: var(--ink-3); margin-top: 18px; }
    h2 { margin-top: 40px; }
    ul { padding-left: 20px; max-width: var(--measure); }
    li { margin-bottom: 8px; }
  </style>
</Base>
